        "original_id": "501fb875-c796-5fdc-b156-df08ba233b6b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hong Kong\n- Buildings: AIA Central, AIG Tower, Furama Hong Kong Hotel\n- Companies: AIA Group\n- Events: 4th Hong Kong Film Awards\n\nFacts:\n- The 4th Hong Kong Film Awards took place on 13 April 1985 at the Furama Hong Kong Hotel in Hong Kong and honored the best films of 1984.\n- The site of the former Furama Hong Kong Hotel is now occupied by the AIA Central office building.\n- AIA Central, formerly called AIG Tower, is a 185-metre, 37-storey skyscraper in Hong Kong that was completed in 2005.\n- AIA Central serves as the headquarters of AIA Group.\n- AIA Group is the largest independent public listed pan-Asian life insurance group.",
